<title>CANADA: Foreigners sell Canada securities in August.</title>
<headline>Foreigners sell Canada securities in August.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investors sold a net C$398.0 million Canadian securities in August, after selling a net C$1.27 billion in July, revised from buying C$174 million, Statistics Canada said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Canadian residents bought a net C$1.15 billion of foreign securities after buying C$2.38 billion in July.</p>
<p>Foreign investments in Canadian securities (blns of dollars)</p>
<p>				   Aug	 July	Year to date</p>
<p>    Total		    -0.398     -1.27	 8.49</p>
<p>    Bonds		    -0.498     -0.49	 5.28</p>
<p>    Money mkt paper	 0.32	-1.18	-3.15</p>
<p>    Stocks		   -0.22	 0.41	 6.36</p>
<p>Canadian investment in foreign securities (blns of dollars)</p>
<p>				   Aug	 July	Year to date</p>
<p>    Total		    -1.15	-2.38	 -9.10</p>
<p>    Bonds		    -0.06	-1.48	 -0.200</p>
<p>    Stocks		   -1.15	-0.90	 -8.90</p>
<p>(A minus sign indicates more purchases from than sales of securities to non-residents, i.e. an outflow of money from Canada, Statistics Canada said.).</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Balance of Payments Division, Don Granger at 613-951-1864.)</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745</p>
